# 1. Component Column — Display Fix

## Background

The current Component column in the Deployment table displays:
- Microservice name
- Namespace name
- Blue/Green deployment badge

All three items are stacked, causing each row to consume excessive vertical space and making the table harder to scan.

## Problem Statement

The component column is showing too much information vertically. The namespace is redundant at the component row level since the namespace is already selected globally. The Blue/Green badge needs to remain but should be repositioned.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-1.1 | Display only the **microservice name** inside the Component column. |
| FR-1.2 | Remove the namespace name from the Component column entirely. |
| FR-1.3 | Display the **Blue/Green deployment badge** inline, immediately to the right of the microservice name, on the same line. |
| FR-1.4 | Badge styling must remain consistent with existing Blue/Green indicator styling. |
| FR-1.5 | No other column, row, or section should be affected. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-1.1
GIVEN the Deployment table is loaded
WHEN a user views the Component column
THEN only the microservice name is displayed
AND the namespace name is NOT shown in that column

AC-1.2
GIVEN the Deployment table is loaded
WHEN a user views the Component column
THEN the Blue or Green deployment badge appears inline
immediately to the right of the microservice name
on the same single line

AC-1.3
GIVEN the Blue/Green badge is displayed inline
WHEN the user views the row
THEN row height is compact and not expanded by stacked elements

AC-1.4
GIVEN the change is applied
WHEN other modules are reviewed
THEN no other table, column, or section is affected
```

## Edge Cases

- If Blue/Green value is missing or null → show microservice name only, no badge rendered
- If microservice name is very long → truncate with ellipsis, show full name in tooltip

