# 2. Release Branch Resolution — Fix

## Background

Fix Version format used in this application:

```
26.7.4 (July 26 – August 1, 2026)
```

Breakdown:
- `26` → Year 2026
- `7` → Month July
- `4` → Fourth release of that month
- `(July 26 – August 1, 2026)` → The valid date range for this release

The release branch must fall **within this date range (inclusive of both boundary dates)**.  
Among all qualifying branches, the one with the **highest release number** must be selected.

## Problem Statement

The release branch shown in the Deployment Section is incorrect. The existing release branch resolution logic (used in other sections via Release Calendar) is either not being called, or is being called incorrectly in this section.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-2.1 | **Reuse the existing release branch resolution service** — do NOT create a new implementation. |
| FR-2.2 | The release branch must fall within the date range declared in the Fix Version. |
| FR-2.3 | Both boundary dates of the range are **inclusive** (e.g., July 26 and August 1 are both valid). |
| FR-2.4 | Among all qualifying branches within the date range, select the one with the **highest release sequence number**. |
| FR-2.5 | The resolved release branch must be used throughout the Deployment Section for all components. |
| FR-2.6 | Resolution must be triggered on Force Refresh. |
| FR-2.7 | Log the resolved branch at INFO level, including the fix version and date range used. |

## Business Rules

```
Fix Version:  26.7.4 (July 26 – August 1, 2026)

Date range:   2026-07-26  →  2026-08-01 (inclusive)

Qualifying release branches within range:
  release/26.07.26.rel  ✅
  release/26.07.28.rel  ✅  ← Highest — SELECTED
  release/26.08.01.rel  ✅

Outside range:
  release/26.07.25.rel  ❌  (before range)
  release/26.08.02.rel  ❌  (after range)
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-2.1
GIVEN Fix Version is "26.7.4 (July 26 – August 1, 2026)"
WHEN the Deployment Section performs a Force Refresh
THEN the existing release branch resolution service is invoked
AND the resolved branch falls within July 26 – August 1, 2026 (inclusive)

AC-2.2
GIVEN multiple qualifying branches exist within the date range
WHEN the resolution service selects the branch
THEN the branch with the highest release sequence number is selected

AC-2.3
GIVEN the release branch is resolved
WHEN displayed in the Deployment table
THEN the correct branch is shown for all components

AC-2.4
GIVEN a branch outside the date range exists
WHEN the resolution runs
THEN that branch is NOT selected regardless of its release number

AC-2.5
GIVEN no qualifying branch is found within the range
WHEN the resolution completes
THEN an appropriate error/warning message is displayed
AND the component status is marked as "Unable to Validate"

AC-2.6
GIVEN the existing resolution service is used
WHEN the change is deployed
THEN no other module using the same service is affected
```

## Edge Cases

- Fix Version has no date range annotation → log warning, show "Unable to Validate"
- Date range spans two months → both months' branches are valid candidates
- Only one branch exists within range → select it regardless of sequence number

