# 3. Kubernetes Branch Name — Display Normalization

## Background

Kubernetes labels return branch names in a hyphenated format:

```
release-26-07-28-release
```

The actual release branch naming convention used everywhere else in the application is:

```
release/26.07.28.rel
```

## Problem Statement

The raw Kubernetes label value is being displayed directly in the UI without transformation, making it inconsistent with all other branch name references across the application.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-3.1 | Transform the Kubernetes raw branch label to standard branch format before displaying. |
| FR-3.2 | Transformation must happen at the **display/mapping layer only** — do NOT alter the raw stored value. |
| FR-3.3 | The raw Kubernetes value must still be persisted as-is in the database. |
| FR-3.4 | Transformation applies only within the Deployment Section UI display. |

## Transformation Rule

```
Raw Kubernetes Label:    release-26-07-28-release
                              ↓ Transform
Display Value:           release/26.07.28.rel

Rule:
  - Replace leading "release-" with "release/"
  - Replace hyphens between date parts with dots
  - Replace trailing "-release" with ".rel"

Pattern:
  release-{YY}-{MM}-{DD}-release  →  release/{YY}.{MM}.{DD}.rel
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-3.1
GIVEN Kubernetes returns branch label "release-26-07-28-release"
WHEN the Deployment table renders the K8s Branch column
THEN the displayed value is "release/26.07.28.rel"

AC-3.2
GIVEN the raw K8s label is transformed for display
WHEN the raw value is retrieved from the database
THEN it remains stored as "release-26-07-28-release" (untransformed)

AC-3.3
GIVEN an unexpected or non-standard K8s branch format is returned
WHEN the transformation fails to match the pattern
THEN the raw value is displayed as-is
AND a console/log warning is emitted

AC-3.4
GIVEN the transformation is applied
WHEN other modules read the K8s branch value from DB
THEN no other module is affected by this display-only change
```

## Edge Cases

- Null or empty K8s branch label → show `—` (em-dash) in UI
- Branch label does not match expected pattern → display raw value, log warning
- Multiple segments or non-standard suffixes → display raw value, log warning

