# 6. Commits Behind Calculation — Merge Commit Exclusion

## Background

The "Commits Behind" value indicates how many non-deployed commits exist on the release branch after the Kubernetes deployment SHA. This count must only reflect meaningful code commits — merge commits are administrative and do not represent actual code changes.

## Problem Statement

The current commits-behind calculation may not be excluding merge commits, leading to inflated or inaccurate behind-counts.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-6.1 | When calculating how many commits the Kubernetes deployment is behind the latest release branch, **exclude all merge commits** from the count. |
| FR-6.2 | Identify the Kubernetes deployed SHA on the release branch commit list. |
| FR-6.3 | Count only **non-merge commits** that appear after the deployed SHA. |
| FR-6.4 | Store the resulting count in the `commits_behind` column. |

## Calculation Logic

```
Release branch commit list (newest → oldest):

  SHA-A  [Merge Commit]     ← EXCLUDED from count
  SHA-B  [Regular Commit]   ← COUNT (1)
  SHA-C  [Regular Commit]   ← COUNT (2)
  SHA-D  [Merge Commit]     ← EXCLUDED from count
  SHA-E  [Regular Commit]   ← KUBERNETES DEPLOYED HERE

  Commits Behind = 2
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-6.1
GIVEN the release branch has the following commits after the K8s deployed SHA:
  - 1 merge commit
  - 2 regular commits
WHEN the commits behind count is calculated
THEN the result is 2 (merge commit excluded)

AC-6.2
GIVEN all commits after the K8s SHA are merge commits only
WHEN the commits behind count is calculated
THEN the result is 0
AND the status shows "Valid Deployment"

AC-6.3
GIVEN the K8s SHA is not found in the release branch commit history
WHEN the calculation runs
THEN commits_behind is set to null or -1
AND the deployment status shows "Unable to Validate"

AC-6.4
GIVEN the K8s SHA matches the latest non-merge commit
WHEN the calculation runs
THEN commits_behind = 0
AND status shows "Valid Deployment"
```

