# 7. Deployment Status — Single Message Format

## Background

Currently, the Deployment Section shows multiple status indicators per component row. The UI must be simplified to show a single, clear, human-readable status message.

## Problem Statement

Multiple status badges or flags clutter each row. Users need one clear statement that tells them the deployment state.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-7.1 | Replace all multiple status indicators with a **single status message** per component row. |
| FR-7.2 | Status message must be determined by priority order (see Business Rules below). |
| FR-7.3 | Status must be stored in `deployment_status` and `validation_message` columns. |

## Business Rules — Status Priority Order

Evaluate conditions in this exact order. Use the **first matching condition**.

```
Priority 1 — Unable to Validate
  Condition:  K8s commit not found on release branch
              OR release branch could not be resolved
              OR GitHub fetch failed
  Message:    "Unable to Validate"
  Style:      Grey / Neutral

Priority 2 — Older Branch
  Condition:  K8s branch does not match resolved release branch
              (branch cut not done or component on previous release)
  Message:    "Older Branch"
  Style:      Orange / Warning

Priority 3 — X Commits Behind
  Condition:  commits_behind > 0
  Message:    "{N} commit(s) behind release branch. Redeployment recommended."
  Style:      Amber / Warning

Priority 4 — Valid Deployment
  Condition:  K8s branch matches release branch
              AND commits_behind = 0
  Message:    "Valid Deployment"
  Style:      Green / Success
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-7.1
GIVEN the K8s branch matches the release branch AND commits_behind = 0
WHEN the status is rendered
THEN only "Valid Deployment" is shown in green

AC-7.2
GIVEN the K8s branch does NOT match the resolved release branch
WHEN the status is rendered
THEN only "Older Branch" is shown in orange

AC-7.3
GIVEN the K8s branch matches AND commits_behind = 3
WHEN the status is rendered
THEN only "3 commit(s) behind release branch. Redeployment recommended." is shown in amber

AC-7.4
GIVEN the release branch could not be resolved
WHEN the status is rendered
THEN only "Unable to Validate" is shown in grey

AC-7.5
GIVEN any component row
WHEN the status column is rendered
THEN exactly ONE status message is visible — no multiple badges or combined indicators

AC-7.6
GIVEN an "Older Branch" condition
WHEN the K8s branch is also behind
THEN "Older Branch" takes priority (Priority 2 wins over Priority 3)
```

