# 8. Scrum Teams & Stories — Display in Table

## Background

The database already stores, per component, the list of associated Scrum Teams and Stories. This data must be surfaced in the Deployment table using the same compact display pattern used in the Branch Cut Validation section.

## Problem Statement

The Deployment table currently does not display scrum teams or stories per component, forcing users to cross-reference with other sections.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-8.1 | Add a **Scrum Teams** column to the Deployment table. |
| FR-8.2 | Add a **Stories** column to the Deployment table. |
| FR-8.3 | Display **1–2 items inline**, followed by a **`+N` badge** for remaining items. |
| FR-8.4 | Hovering the `+N` badge opens a **tooltip** listing all remaining items. |
| FR-8.5 | Fetch this data from the existing database records — do NOT call iTrack again. |
| FR-8.6 | The display behavior must match the exact pattern used in Branch Cut Validation. |

## Display Pattern

```
Scrum Teams column (example — 4 teams):
  Team Alpha  Team Beta  +2 ▼
                              └─ tooltip: Team Gamma, Team Delta

Stories column (example — 6 stories):
  SPT-1001  SPT-1002  +4 ▼
                          └─ tooltip: SPT-1003, SPT-1004, SPT-1005, SPT-1006
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-8.1
GIVEN a component has 1 scrum team
WHEN the Deployment table renders
THEN the single team name is shown inline with no +N badge

AC-8.2
GIVEN a component has 2 scrum teams
WHEN the Deployment table renders
THEN both team names are shown inline with no +N badge

AC-8.3
GIVEN a component has 4 scrum teams
WHEN the Deployment table renders
THEN 2 team names are shown inline and "+2" badge is shown
AND hovering the "+2" badge shows a tooltip with the remaining 2 team names

AC-8.4
GIVEN a component has 6 stories
WHEN the Deployment table renders
THEN 2 story IDs are shown inline and "+4" badge is shown
AND hovering "+4" reveals the remaining 4 story IDs in a tooltip

AC-8.5
GIVEN a component has no associated scrum teams
WHEN the Deployment table renders
THEN the Scrum Teams column shows "—" (em-dash)

AC-8.6
GIVEN a component has no associated stories
WHEN the Deployment table renders
THEN the Stories column shows "—" (em-dash)

AC-8.7
GIVEN the data is fetched
WHEN the backend processes the request
THEN scrum teams and stories are loaded from the existing DB records
AND NO new iTrack API call is made
```

