# 10. Dropdown Filter — Data-Driven Values (Branch Cut Validation + Deployment)

## Background

Currently, filter dropdowns (such as Scrum Team filter) show all possible values regardless of what data is currently displayed in the table. This causes confusion — users see filter options for teams that have no records in the current filtered view.

**This change applies to BOTH:**
- Branch Cut Validation section
- Deployment Section

## Problem Statement

When a user applies a filter (e.g., "Pending Only"), the table shows a reduced set of rows. But the Scrum Team dropdown still shows all teams including those with no pending items — these are irrelevant options and create a confusing UX.

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-10.1 | All filter dropdowns must derive their option list from the **currently displayed table rows only**. |
| FR-10.2 | When a primary filter changes the displayed data, all dependent dropdowns must **recalculate their options**. |
| FR-10.3 | If a previously selected dropdown value no longer exists in the new option set, **reset that dropdown to "All"**. |
| FR-10.4 | This rule applies to: Scrum Team filter in Branch Cut Validation, Scrum Team filter in Deployment Section. |
| FR-10.5 | The computation of dropdown options must happen on the **frontend from rendered data** — not from a new backend call. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-10.1
GIVEN the Deployment table shows 10 rows (teams A, B, C, D present)
WHEN the user applies "Show Invalid Only" and only 4 rows remain (teams A, B only)
THEN the Scrum Team dropdown recalculates and shows only Team A and Team B
AND Team C and Team D are removed from the dropdown options

AC-10.2
GIVEN the user has "Team C" selected in the Scrum Team filter
WHEN a new primary filter is applied that removes all Team C rows
THEN the Scrum Team dropdown resets to "All Teams" automatically

AC-10.3
GIVEN the Branch Cut Validation section has the same dropdown behavior
WHEN a primary filter changes visible rows
THEN the Scrum Team dropdown in Branch Cut Validation also recalculates correctly

AC-10.4
GIVEN all rows are visible (no filters active)
WHEN the Scrum Team dropdown is opened
THEN all teams from all rows are listed

AC-10.5
GIVEN the dropdown recalculation is implemented
WHEN a new backend fetch runs
THEN the dropdown options recalculate from the new result set

AC-10.6
GIVEN the change is applied
WHEN the Branch Cut Validation or Deployment section is tested
THEN no unnecessary backend calls are made to recalculate dropdown options
```

